 ### Fixed

+- `OrchestratorHooks.onError` now fires on every rejection inside a turn, not only when the thrown value is an `Error` instance. Rejections that are not already an `Error` — such as a thrown string, plain object, or `undefined` — are wrapped in an `Error` with a readable `message` and the original value preserved on `error.cause`, while existing `Error` instances continue to reach `onError` unchanged and the caller still receives the original rejection verbatim. **Migration note**: if your `onError` hook counts failures or pages an operator, it will now observe non-`Error` rejections that were previously dropped silently; read `error.cause` when you need the raw non-`Error` value.
 - `onError` and `afterSession` hooks now fire when `beforeSession` throws, matching the guarantee the hook names imply. Previously, a throw from `beforeSession` escaped the `try`/`finally` block entirely, so neither hook ran. **Migration note**: if your `afterSession` hook assumed it would only be called after a full session turn, it will now also be called when `beforeSession` itself fails — the hook can inspect the session to detect this case (no entries beyond the initial user message will have been processed).

